      "sourceTextSha256": "0327f8ee8aa71f780c049bd04d950f2cb8f2e39af9f4d0ceaaeab20c5d02d9ab",
      "text": "Day 13 · Breakfast. City tour with a guide (4 hours) through a capital of elegant architecture, museums, galleries and theatres: the old district of La Boca, historic San Telmo with its bars, restaurants and antiques market on Plaza Dorrego, Plaza de Mayo with the Casa Rosada, associated with Eva Perón, the 67-metre Obelisk on Avenida 9 de Julio, the elegant Recoleta district with its famous cemetery and the colonial-style church of El Pilar, modern Puerto Madero and the Lezama and Tres de Febrero parks.\n\nEvening · Tango show with dinner (without guide). Born in the city’s port neighbourhoods among immigrants and working people, tango has become one of the most sensual dances in the world; a menu of traditional dishes with excellent Argentine wines completes this romantic evening.",
